STEP 8 — Reliable ARP + Bidirectional Forwarding
🎯 Goal

In Step 7, we proved:

h1 → s1 → s2 → s4 → h2

works with 0% packet loss.

But the controller currently handles ARP by flooding it:

ARP → FLOOD

Your topology contains a loop, so we don't want uncontrolled ARP flooding affecting our future latency/congestion measurements. The previous project notes specifically identified this as the next issue to fix.

So Step 8 will make ARP handling controlled while preserving our NetworkX routing.

